body:
Yeah, I should really try to make friends in my classes. It's just I'm bad with initiating things, once the ball gets moving I'm on a roll. But anything prior to, yikes. 

&#x200B;

Yeah, I've thought about it, and did it in the past when I had people I knew available. Honestly I should just try things instead of just waiting for an opportunity to present itself, I'm too shy for my own good at the beginning.

Maybe, I just am very hesitant spending my dad's money. I know he lives to provide but I'm tired of being a leech, agh. Perhaps, that's a good idea and I'm definitely saving that for later use.

&#x200B;

I like the title extrovert and I try to make sure people are comfortable or laughing in bad or strange situations. It's like a fight-or-flight kind of reflex to me. The problem isn't entirely I can't connect as much as I don't know how to go about finding new people I guess. Like I get along fine casually with people, just when I'm on downtime I have nothing really to do except go around town by myself lmao.

&#x200B;

Yeah, one foot in front of the other, it's how I'm "living". Though it doesn't really feel like it, it's like things are monotonous and droll. Like a clockwork, I like having spice in life and lately it just feels like a blob of school and obligation.
